---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Research — A3S Labs" description="Applied machine learning, computer vision, forecasting and experimental systems from A3S Labs.">
  <section class="page-hero section-pad">
    <div class="shell page-hero-grid">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span>RESEARCH</span><span>A3S / 02</span></p>
      <div><h1>Models attached to real signals.</h1><p>Research work is most useful when the task, data, evaluation and deployment path remain visible. The aim is not to decorate products with AI; it is to build measurable systems around difficult signals.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-pad section-rule">
    <div class="shell research-deep-grid">
      <article class="accent-honey">
        <span>01 / MULTIMODAL HIVE INTELLIGENCE</span>
        <h2>BeeUnity</h2>
        <p>Queen-presence detection begins with hive audio: WAV samples are converted to mel spectrograms, a CNN is tuned and class thresholds are calibrated from validation precision-recall behavior. A second pipeline combines weather, NDVI, floral context and hive telemetry for stress and yield modelling.</p>
        <div class="tag-row"><span>TensorFlow</span><span>PyTorch</span><span>NDVI</span><span>FastAPI</span></div>
        <a href="/case-studies/beeunity">Research case study ↗</a>
      </article>

      <article class="accent-violet">
        <span>02 / 3D COMPUTER VISION</span>
        <h2>Vesuvius surface detection</h2>
        <p>The task is 3D papyrus-surface segmentation from CT scan chunks of carbonized Herculaneum scrolls. Evaluation is topology-aware: surface proximity is not enough if the prediction bridges separate sheets, creates holes or breaks one sheet into disconnected components.</p>
        <div class="tag-row"><span>3D segmentation</span><span>Surface Dice</span><span>TopoScore</span><span>VOI</span></div>
        <a href="https://github.com/simlexx-k/vesuvius-surface-detection" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Repository ↗</a>
      </article>

      <article class="accent-cyan">
        <span>03 / FORECASTING + CONTEXT</span>
        <h2>From classification to downstream decisions</h2>
        <p>The research pattern extends beyond a single classifier: environmental features, rolling statistics, calibrated probabilities and forecast outputs are staged so model results can feed APIs, dashboards and later decision-support workflows.</p>
        <div class="tag-row"><span>XGBoost</span><span>scikit-learn</span><span>time series</span><span>calibration</span></div>
        <a href="https://github.com/simlexx-k/QueenBeeAcoustics" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Inspect pipeline ↗</a>
      </article>

      <article class="accent-blue">
        <span>04 / DATA SCIENCE PRACTICE</span>
        <h2>Evaluation is part of the system</h2>
        <p>Across classification, graph work, regression, NLP and exploratory analysis, the recurring concern is the same: choose metrics that expose the failure mode, preserve reproducibility, and avoid turning confidence scores into unsupported certainty.</p>
        <div class="tag-row"><span>evaluation</span><span>graphs</span><span>NLP</span><span>regression</span></div>
        <a href="https://github.com/simlexx-k?tab=repositories" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Browse research code ↗</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-pad capability-band">
    <div class="shell">
      <header class="section-heading split-heading">
        <div><p class="section-kicker">Research method</p><h2>A repeatable path from signal to evidence.</h2></div>
        <p>Different datasets require different models, but the workflow should still make uncertainty, evaluation and reproducibility visible.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="method-strip">
        <article><span>01</span><h3>Define the signal</h3><p>Identify what is directly observed, what is inferred and which labels or measurements can actually support the task.</p></article>
        <article><span>02</span><h3>Build the pipeline</h3><p>Make preprocessing, feature construction, splits, training and artifact generation repeatable rather than notebook-only state.</p></article>
        <article><span>03</span><h3>Measure the failure</h3><p>Use class-aware, topology-aware or calibration-aware metrics when aggregate accuracy would hide the important error.</p></article>
        <article><span>04</span><h3>Leave a serving path</h3><p>Export artifacts and define an API or product boundary so useful results can move beyond experimentation.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-pad section-rule">
    <div class="shell narrative-grid">
      <div><p class="section-kicker">Current emphasis</p><h2>Reproducibility before novelty claims.</h2></div>
      <div class="narrative-copy">
        <p>BeeUnity already connects tuned acoustic models, contextual features, FastAPI serving and report generation. The Vesuvius work adds a different constraint: correct geometry must also be topologically right. Together they represent the kind of applied research A3S Labs should publish—specific tasks, explicit metrics and inspectable code.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/builds">See related build milestones ↗</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
